<!--
  ANI-KUTA notification small icon (D-474)
  Glyph: the kawaii mascot mouth simplified to a bold monochrome mark.
  The white shape is the open-mouth cavity with the mascot's characteristic
  up-turned corner spikes; knocked out of it (alpha cutouts, fillType evenOdd)
  are (1) the big lobe-shaped tongue low in the mouth and (2) the two small
  upper fangs hanging from the lip. Pure white #FFFFFFFF on transparent, no
  tint, no gradients: the system alpha-masks and recolors notification small
  icons, so color is supplied by the notification builder (Material You /
  colorControlNormal), never by this file. Designed for a 24dp grid with
  ~2dp side padding; all sub-paths are closed and the fang cutouts hug the
  upper-lip curve (quadratic approximations of the lip cubic) so they read
  as notches, never as floating specks.
-->
